DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ppttssnnaammee() function returns the name of the slave pseudoterminal de‐
       vice corresponding to the master referred to by the file descriptor _f_d.

       The  ppttssnnaammee__rr() function is the reentrant equivalent of ppttssnnaammee().  It
       returns the name of the slave pseudoterminal device  as  a  null‐termi‐
       nated string in the buffer pointed to by _b_u_f.  The _s_i_z_e argument speci‐
       fies the number of bytes available in _b_u_f.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On  success,  ppttssnnaammee() returns a pointer to a string in static storage
       which will be overwritten by subsequent calls.  This pointer  must  not
       be freed.  On failure, NULL is returned.

       On  success, ppttssnnaammee__rr() returns 0.  On failure, an error number is re‐
       turned to indicate the error.

